From 79f93fb29a732faa546255e05cbed41ae8f1ba6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:06:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/21] video: console: report damage when showing the cursor

With CONFIG_VIDEO_DAMAGE, video_sync() only flushes the dirty rectangle
reported for a frame.  Every vidconsole write path reports damage except
the console cursor: console_set_cursor_visible() writes the cursor
straight into the frame buffer without a video_damage() call, so the
cursor region stayed dirty and was never flushed -- a blinking cursor
was invisible until some other output dirtied the same lines.

Report the cursor rectangle when it is shown or hidden.

Signed-off-by: Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>
---
 drivers/video/console_normal.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/console_normal.c b/drivers/video/console_normal.c
index 6dc0a6eaf9d..6d450a8c738 100644
--- a/drivers/video/console_normal.c
+++ b/drivers/video/console_normal.c
@@ -121,6 +121,12 @@ static int console_set_cursor_visible(struct udevice *dev, bool visible,
 		return -ENOSYS;
 
 	x += index * fontdata->width;
+	/*
+	 * The cursor is written straight into the frame buffer below;
+	 * report the rectangle so video_sync() flushes only these lines.
+	 */
+	video_damage(vid, x, y, VIDCONSOLE_CURSOR_WIDTH,
+		     vc_priv->y_charsize);
 	start = vid_priv->fb + y * vid_priv->line_length + x * pbytes;
 
 	/* place the cursor 1 pixel before the start of the next char */
-- 
